TNT - Hostmode Terminal for TNC
==============================

TNT is a packet-radio hostmode terminal, originally developed by Mark Wahl.
See AUTHORS, COPYING, NEWS and the doc directory for contributors, licensing,
release history and operating documentation.

Building
--------

Requirements:
  - C compiler such as GCC or Clang
  - CMake 3.20 or newer
  - Make, or optionally Ninja
  - ncurses development headers and libraries
  - system gettext tools for translations
  - dialog for the optional interactive setup scripts

Debian, Ubuntu and Raspberry Pi OS:

    sudo apt install build-essential cmake ninja-build libncurses-dev gettext dialog

Fedora:

    sudo dnf install gcc cmake ninja-build ncurses-devel gettext dialog

Arch Linux:

    sudo pacman -S base-devel cmake ninja ncurses gettext dialog

Configure, compile and test:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    cmake --build build --parallel 2
    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

Add -G Ninja when configuring to use Ninja instead of Make. Generated files
and executables stay in build/. Autoconf and Automake are no longer used.

Installation
------------

    cmake --install build

Use suitable permissions for the chosen prefix. Installation does not start
a service or overwrite an active tnt.ini; example files use .ex suffixes.
To install privately with runtime data under your home directory:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
      -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$HOME/.local" \
      -DTNT_LOCALSTATEDIR="$HOME/.local/var"

Set paths at configuration time. Runtime state otherwise defaults to /var,
even with a custom prefix. The interactive tnt_setup.de, tnt_setup.en and
tnt_setup.fr scripts can be run manually after installation.

Common options
--------------

    -DTNT_SERIAL=OFF       Disable serial/soft-TNC device handling
    -DTNT_SOUND=OFF        Disable sound
    -DTNT_NLS=OFF          Disable translations and gettext dependency
    -DTNT_LANGUAGE=de      Default configuration language (en, de, fr)
    -DTNT_AX25K2=ON        Enable modern Linux kernel AX.25 (requires libax25)
    -DTNT_AX25K=ON         Enable legacy AX.25 library interface
    -DTNT_HIBAUD=ON        Enable Linux high-baud-rate support
    -DTNT_GENUSER=ON       Enable legacy Unix user generation (off by default)
    -DTNT_FLAT=ON          Install everything under PREFIX/tnt

The historical DPBOXT mode was already broken and is not supported.
System gettext is used; there is no bundled-gettext fallback.
Use Unix user generation cautiously and see AX25-NOTES before enabling
kernel AX.25 support.

Raspberry Pi / ARM
------------------

The same CMake commands apply to Raspberry Pi OS. CI covers native amd64
and arm64 Linux, plus 32-bit ARMv7 armhf under QEMU. Debian packaging also
supports cross-compilation; see BUILD.md and packaging/README.packages.

AX25UDP soft-TNC mode uses soft_tnc 3. Set device to host:port or to
localport@host:port when a fixed local UDP source port is required.

Configuration
-------------

For private settings, create ~/.tnt and copy the configuration files there.
TNT searches ~/.tnt/tnt.ini, ~/.tnt/.tntrc, the current directory, the compiled
installation configuration directory, and finally /etc/tnt.ini. The -i option
selects an explicit file. TNTC uses its corresponding tntc.ini configuration.

See BUILD.md for feature mappings from the old configure options, installation
paths, strict compiler checks, tests and the current terminal behavior.
Runtime documentation and translated help files are in doc/ and examples/.
